+    // The attract fade/transition scenes (off14 0x06036610 = f_232610, scenes 3,5,7,9,15,...) advance
+    // only when their content task reaches its completion state, which requires the transition-timeline
+    // interpreter f_2463c8 (cart 0x243628, rt 0x0604a3c8) to run to end-of-script and set the content
+    // entity unk3c bit3. That interpreter early-returns (switch on 0x06098564: case 0) unless
+    // 0x06098564 != 0, which f_22a8d8 (cart 0x22a8d8) only sets when the "2 players armed" flag
+    // 0x06098670 == 0 (pure attract, both channels). Under the harness 0x06098670 is left = 1 (set
+    // once at VB201 by f_201cae, guarded by 0x06000798 bit5 / 0x0609880c==1), so the timeline never
+    // advances and the reel stalls at scene 3. Semantically 0x06098670 should be 0 during attract
+    // (no players). This holds it 0 so the real completion path runs. NOT a force of the completion
+    // bit (director unk3c bit0) -- it only restores the attract arm-flag the real path reads.
+    // SUPERSEDED (2026-10-20, coin_arm_and_reel.md): the coin-path permanent park is now fixed
+    // faithfully in deliver_coin (the real coin-detect credit-byte gate), so this force is no
+    // longer needed for the coin path. Kept default-off for the completion-mechanism diagnostic.
+    static const char* attractarm = std::getenv("STV_ATTRACTARM");
+    if (attractarm) {
+        st32(0x06098670u, 0);
+    }
+
+    // STV_STARTFLAG (diagnostic, default off): the old pre-coin behaviour -- raise the player
+    // start-present flag 0x06098688/89 directly, which drives the game out of the attract freeze
+    // into the start/continue sequence WITHOUT a credit (reaches the demo continue flow, not a
+    // paid round). Kept for comparison; see notes/port/stv_input_gameplay_status.md. The faithful
+    // path leaves this off: START is a panel action and only begins a game when a credit exists.
+    static const char* startflag = std::getenv("STV_STARTFLAG");
+    // STV_PANELBTN (experimental, default off): inject face/direction tokens as the ONE cooked
+    // input bit that is verified decodable here -- bit0 of the cooked "a-control-is-pressed" word
+    // 0x0609879A (= MU16(g_06098794,6)), read as "&3 => pressed" by e.g. func_0201f20 state 1 and
+    // the scene-skip handlers. This lets a --stvinput timeline satisfy "press to continue/skip"
+    // gates. It writes the cooked word directly (bypassing the game's panel decoder) because the
+    // full panel-buffer direction/button bit map is NOT resolved -- see the notes file. Default off
+    // so the baseline is byte-identical. The per-button/direction identity is intentionally NOT
+    // faked: every face/dir token collapses to the same verified "pressed" bit.
